    "## 2. Reliability diagrams\n",
    "\n",
    "Loans are sorted by predicted risk and cut into ten equal-size groups. For each group the plot shows the average predicted default rate (across) against the actual default rate (up), with a 95% interval for the actual rate. Perfect calibration is the diagonal. Both axes are on a log scale because most default rates are small."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "ed2da5eb",
   "metadata": {
