    "## 5. What I see\n",
    "\n",
    "In-time the models are calibrated: predicted / actual is 0.98 to 1.00, the calibration slope is 0.94 to 0.98 (intervals contain 1) and the binomial test finds nothing wrong (p = 0.53 to 0.99). Out of time they are too low and more so each year. For the logistic model predicted / actual is 0.74 (2005), 0.42 (2006) and 0.18 (2007), for boosting 0.69, 0.47 and 0.21, and the binomial test rejects calibration every time (p below 0.0001). For the logistic model I'd have to push the predictions up by 0.33, 0.93 and 1.89 on the log-odds scale, so the odds of default are about 1.4, 2.5 and 6.6 times what the model says.\n",
