    "- A bank might have earlier signals than a complete two-year outcome (for example early delinquency of the newest loans). I didn't test that, so my delayed correction is a rough, pessimistic stand-in.\n",
    "- Reliability and ECE are noisy for the lowest-risk groups, which have few defaults. The hold-out has only 209.\n",
    "- The idea that stress squeezed the differences between loans (slope below 1) is my reading of the numbers, not something I tested.\n",
    "- I haven't touched whether uncertainty from Bayesian or ensemble models could warn about the shift. That part of the project title is still open."
   ]
